<title>USA: UAW strikes GM's Indianapolis stamping plant.</title>
<headline>UAW strikes GM's Indianapolis stamping plant.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Auto Workers union unleashed a local strike against General Motors Corp.'s Indianapolis metal stamping plant Tuesday that threatened to paralyze much of the company's light truck production.</p>
<p>A GM spokesman confirmed that members of UAW Local 23 went on strike shortly after 6 p.m. EST. The Indiana facility employs about 2,750 hourly workers and produces fenders, doors, hoods and other major steel stampings for about nine GM truck assembly plants.</p>
</text>
